# What not to upload to Cloud Foundry. Everything the app needs at runtime is either in the
# push or installed at staging; the local node_modules must never travel, since it holds
# Windows or macOS builds of better-sqlite3 and of the Copilot CLI and staging installs the
# Linux ones itself. web/dist does travel: the SPA is built here, so staging only installs.
.git/
.github/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# runtime data and secrets
data/
data-*/
**/data-smoke/
**/data-demo/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.env
.env.*
deploy/backups/
*.log

# build and authoring by-products with no part in the running app
docs/html/
docs/brand/
**/.vite/
**/coverage/
